---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBaby Sleep Answers (https://www.babysleepanswers.com/baby)\nciteturn75search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; \n\nImage: Image Description\n\n#### Part 2: Tools\n\n###### \n\nThen you’ll receive specific tools to take that information and optimize practices to help your baby start getting the sleep that they (and you) need.\n\n* I will hand you the tools to create their perfect, unique, and flexible schedule\n\n* You will learn the what, where, and why of a perfect sleep environment\n\n* You will have the tools to create your own unique sleep goal and achieve it at your own pace.\n\nImage: Image Description\n\n#### Part 3: Troubleshooting\n\n###### \n\nFinally, the last part is to troubleshoot, to continue to understand the ups and downs of issues that disrupt baby sleep and how to recover from them.\n\nBaby sleep isn’t perfect, so you’ll have the priceless troubleshooting guide to help you navigate:\n\n* Schedule changes and individual needs\n\n* Regressions\n\n* Night weaning when you’re ready\n\n* What to do when baby skips a nap\n\n* How and when to drop a nap\n\nImage: Image Description\n\nImage: Image Description\n\nGet access to our member’s only FB group where you can ask big and small questions every day. No question goes unanswered because it is full of parents who are or have been sleep deprived and are learning with you. You’ll have a home for all your sleep questions and group feedback within 24 hours.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL GET INSIDE\n\n“The course is easy to understand and it was perfectly fit for our needs.”\n\nImage\n\nAndreea Corbu\n\nOctober, 2022\n\n“I strongly believe that Andrea is a genius. The course is easy to understand and it was perfectly fit for our needs. After only one night my baby is sleeping much better and I am confident about what is next. Good job and thank you!”\n\n“So if you’re still wondering whether to do it or not, DO IT. Your future self will thank you.”\n\nImage\n\nNancy Contarino\n\nJune, 2022\n\n“The first time I came across Baby Sleep Answers was on a random Instagram post late one night while I was rocking my baby back to sleep for, what felt like, the hundredth time searching for “baby sleep tips” and I was hooked. At that point I used Andrea’s sleep tips and posts on her page but never actually bought a sleep plan. BUT for my second son, there was no way I was going to put myself through the same late night heartache AND not knowing how to deal with a toddler PLUS an infant that won’t sleep, so I finally bought her plan and WOW, I wish I had done it way sooner with my first son because even though the posts on her page helped me SO much, buying an actual plan and following it was the best thing I did the second time around. #### Frequently Asked Questions\n\nWill this course continue to be updated? And will I have access to future versions?\n\nYes! We are continuously improving and updating our course and once you get it: it’s yours forever! In fact, if there is something you don’t see in the course that you would like to, just email us and we’ll add it!\n\nI’m very busy, how long does it take to get through the course?\n\nTotally depends on you! You could finish it in just a couple of hours and come back to it whenever you need, or you can take it slow, watch all the videos at your pace as you need them, and of course, always come back to them.\n\nCan I use FSA or HSA to pay?\n\nYES! Andrea is a Certified Holistic Drugless Practitioner and as one you can pay for all of our courses and consultations with your FSA or HSA! First Contact your FSA administrator and tell them you’d like to have sleep consultation services covered. They may ask you to ask your pediatrician for a letter of medical necessity, this is easy! Then If you use FSA you may have to prepay and then ask us for a receipt to submit to your FSA administrator. \nImage\n\nKatie Morgan\n\nSeptember, 2022\n\n“After 10 months of having baby still wake every 2 hrs to feed I became desperate for some help. I’m so grateful to have found Andrea’s page, I quickly found her tips and suggestions easy to follow that I decided to purchase her plan. Wow! The amount of information she provided and multiple different styles of training methods I could not be more grateful for. She explains everything so well it’s easy to follow while sleep deprived. Her plans provided gentle methods for me as I was terrified and not willing to do the insanely suggested CIO method everyone and doctor seemed to only recommend. She touches on your own baby’s specific personality and understands there’s not just a one for all method to help baby sleep longer. After 3 nights we were completely sleeping all night, but even after one day I saw a difference. I was beyond skeptical about sleep training and couldn’t pull the plug on any plan for weeks maybe months, but I’m so glad I did with Baby Sleep Answers. I recommend to everyone I know with babies.”\n\n“...this plan has helped us thru every sleep transition so far, as well as helping to navigate teething, sickness, travel, and figuring out how/when to drop naps.”\n\nImage\n\nMaria Robinson\n\n2022\n\n“I originally bought the customized sleep plan when my daughter was 5mo old. We had been struggling with reflux, cosleeping, and it just wasn’t working for any of us. We were able to transition her from cosleeping, to sleeping 8-10hr stretches in her pack n play in our room in 3 nights. Four months later we were ready to transition her to her crib in her own room - our plan was able to help us once again. We still chose to rock her to sleep, but she was sleeping 12-13hr nights with no tears in her own room after 2 nights. This month we finally decided rocking her to sleep wasn’t working for us. Using our same plan, within 1wk our daughter (now 19mo) was falling asleep independently with no tears. All of this to say, this plan has helped us thru every sleep transition so far, as well as helping to navigate teething, sickness, travel, and figuring out how/when to drop naps. Forever grateful for Andrea’s plan and help in our sleep journey!”\n\n“...it’s like Andrea knows our baby and what he’s about to do!”\n\nImage\n\nStefanie Wind\n\nMay 2023\n\n“This course has been extremely helpful for our baby’s sleep! We bought the baby package and love how it includes multiple options and grows with our baby. We had purchased another course and corresponding consultation with a different sleep consultant, but Baby Sleep Answers was more helpful AND less expensive. Our baby still has some hiccups with his sleep but I have always been able to refer to the course pdf and find helpful tips--it’s like Andrea knows our baby and what he’s about to do! I have already recommended this course to my friends who are expecting and I hope they buy it sooner than I did. :) Thanks, Andrea and Joe!!!”\n\n“When I got the plan, I was blown away with all the options in mind that were tailored to my family.”\n\nImage\n\nJessica Frattare\n\nJuly, 2022\n\n“I bought a sleep plan for my 7 month old who had such a hard time sleeping, and doing it independently. Andrea recommended the course for my baby’s age and when purchasing, it asked a bunch of questions so it could be tailored to my child, as well as my schedule, our nursing schedule, and my expectations. When I got the plan, I was blown away with all the options in mind that were tailored to my family. After 3 nights, my baby was sleeping 8 hours straight and falling asleep within 15 minutes. It’s been 2 weeks and she now sleeps about 11-12 hours each night and 1-2 hours for both of her naps, in her crib independently. We are SO thankful for this sleep plan. THANK YOU, ANDREA!”\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAbout Taylor Vanderwolk, Baby Registry Consultant | Taylor-Made Baby Co. (https://www.taylormadebabyco.com/about)\nciteturn75search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; \n\