e\n\nHelp narrowing down the biggest product decisions\n\nFollow-up notes with your next best steps\n\nBook a Registry ConsultLooking for longer-term support? Contact Taylor\n\nTrusted Prep Partners\n\nServices Taylor recommends and works alongside for car seat safety, home childproofing, and newborn sleep.\n\nImage: Lani Car Seats logo\n\n### Lani Car Seats\n\nCPST-certified car seat installation and safety checks, available virtually and in the Phoenix area.\n\nImage: AZ Childproofers logo\n\n### AZ Childproofers\n\nProfessional childproofing assessments and installations for Arizona families.\n\nTiny Toes Newborn Newborn sleep consulting and support for families navigating the fourth trimester.\n\nAs Heard On\n\nBabyQuip: Tiny Travels\n\nPodcast Episode\n\n## Taylor on Baby Gear, Registry Strategy & Real-Life Fit\n\nTaylor joins the BabyQuip team to talk through what actually matters when preparing for a baby, and how to stop letting the gear pile-up steal the joy from early parenthood.\n\nBabyQuip Tiny Travels Podcast – Taylor-Made Baby Co. Episode\n\nOpen in Spotify\n\nClient Stories\n\n## What families say about working with Taylor\n\n“You don’t have to figure this out alone.”\n\nReviews from Taylor’s time at Strolleria\n\nSwipe for more\n\n★★★★★\n\n“Taylor took what could have been a very overwhelming experience and made it so simple and easy. She spent 3+ hours with me as we talked through the pros/cons of each brand and was so patient and kind... Corporate, if you're reading this, time to give Taylor a promotion/raise!”\n\nAmanda M. · Strolleria client\n\n★★★★★\n\n“She listened to what we were looking for, and was so honest and transparent about all of the baby gear we were considering. We ended up buying something completely different than our 'online research' because of her help.”\n\nKathryn G. · Strolleria client\n\n★★★★★\n\n“She is truly a wealth of knowledge and guided us in the right direction based on our individual needs and preferences. ## Baby registry consultant FAQ\n\nThe questions expecting parents ask most, answered straight.\n\nWhat does a baby registry consultant do?+\n\nA baby registry consultant helps expecting parents choose the right strollers, car seats, nursery gear, and baby products for their actual home, lifestyle, and budget. At Taylor-Made Baby Co., Taylor runs one hour virtual consultations that cover your whole registry, so you avoid expensive mistakes, narrow the big decisions, and end up with a list that fits your real life instead of the internet.\n\nHow much does a baby registry consultation cost?+\n\nA registry consultation with Taylor-Made Baby Co. is $75 for a one hour virtual session. That includes personalized gear guidance, help narrowing your biggest product decisions, and written follow up notes with your next best steps. Longer-term planning support is available too, just reach out through the contact form and Taylor will point you to the right level.\n\nIs a baby registry consultation worth it?+\n\nFor most expecting parents, one hour of expert guidance saves several hundred dollars in gear that would have been returned or never used. A consultant helps you skip the common mistakes, like buying a stroller that does not fit your car, registering for things that do not fit your home, or doubling up on items that do the same job. Plenty of clients change their original picks completely once they talk it through.\n\nWhat is a Target Baby Concierge Specialist?+\n\nTarget Baby Concierge Specialists are trained baby gear advisors placed in Target stores through the Baby Concierge program. Taylor is a Gugu Concierge, and it is the same expertise she brings to virtual consultations at Taylor-Made Baby Co.\n\nWhen should I book a baby registry consultation?+\n\nMost families get the most out of a consultation somewhere between weeks 20 and 28. That is early enough to build the registry before baby shower season, but far enough along that you know your due date, home setup, and budget. That said, any stage works, including families who already have a partial registry and want help refining it.\n\nWhat baby gear does a consultation cover?+\n\nA consultation covers stroller selection and compatibility, car seat safety and fit, nursery essentials and setup, sleep gear, feeding equipment, and registry strategy and timing. If you have specific product questions, like comparing two brands or choosing between options, bring them to the session and we will work through them together.\n\nDo I need to have started my registry before booking?+\n\nNo. Some clients show up with a blank registry and build from scratch in the session. Others arrive with a 150 item list and need help cutting it down. Both are completely normal, and both are exactly what the consultation is for. Taylor reviews your intake before you meet so she arrives ready for your situation.\n\nIs the consultation virtual or in person?+\n\nEvery consultation is virtual, held over video call, and available to expecting parents anywhere in the United States. The session is a one hour video call with Taylor, followed by written notes afterward. For families in the Phoenix area, Taylor can also connect you with CPST certified car seat specialists and local baby safety professionals.\n\nFrom the Journal\n\n## Baby gear guidance, straight from Taylor.\n\nRead the Journal→\n\nRegistry Strategy·By Taylor Vanderwolk·48 min read·June 25, 2026\n\n### Best Baby Bottle Washers of 2026: Momcozy D8 vs. Eufy & More\n\nThe bottle washer showdown has a new frontrunner. I'm comparing Momcozy's DeepClean D8, Eufy, Grownsy, Papablic and more to help you choose the right machine for your feeding routine.\n\nRead Article→\n\n[Button: Share][Button: Save]\n\nGear & Safety·By Taylor Vanderwolk·36 min read·June 16, 2026\n\n### Silver Cross Cove 2 Review: Everything Parents Should Know Before Buying\n\nBefore you add the Silver Cross Cove 2 to your registry, here's what actually matters — the fold, real cost, newborn se